## Running the CLI

`@datocms/cli` is a local dependency. Always run from `webpage/`:

```bash
pnpm exec datocms <command> --api-token=<TOKEN>
```

API token: `DATOCMS_FULL_ACCESS_KEY` from `.envrc.localdev_secrets`.

---

## Standard Procedure

### Step 1: Scaffold

**Option A: Manual (most common)**
```bash
pnpm exec datocms migrations:new '<description>' --ts --api-token=<TOKEN>
```

**Option B: Autogenerate from sandbox diff**
```bash
pnpm exec datocms migrations:new '<description>' --ts --autogenerate=<sandbox>:<source-env> --api-token=<TOKEN>
```

### Step 2: Write the Migration

```typescript
import { Client } from '@datocms/cma-client'

export default async function (client: Client) {
  console.log('Create model "YourModel" (`your_model`)')
  const model = await client.itemTypes.create({
    name: 'YourModel',
    api_key: 'your_model',
    collection_appearance: 'table',
  }, { skip_menu_item_creation: true })

  console.log('Create field "Title" (`title`)')
  await client.fields.create(model.id, {
    label: 'Title',
    field_type: 'string',
    api_key: 'title',
    validators: { required: {} },
    appearance: { addons: [], editor: 'single_line', parameters: { heading: true } },
  })
}
```

**Import:** Always use `@datocms/cma-client`. Do NOT use `@datocms/cma-client-node`.

**Base fields for every new CMS section model:**
- `internal_title` (string, required, unique) — editorial-only
- `section_id` (string, required) — HTML `id` for anchor links
- `layout` (string) — visual variant selector

**Localized fields — include ALL locales:**
```typescript
default_value: { en: false, es: null, fr: null, de: null, it: null, pt: null,
  'pt-BR': null, 'en-GB': null, 'es-MX': null, ca: null, pl: null, 'en-ZA': null, 'en-ke': null }
```

**Adding to sections block:** Update the `sections` field on `sections_block` to include the new model's ID.

### Step 3: Test

```bash
# Fresh sandbox
pnpm exec datocms migrations:run --destination=<sandbox-name> --api-token=<TOKEN>

# Re-test after editing (destroy first)
pnpm exec datocms environments:destroy <sandbox-name> --api-token=<TOKEN>
pnpm exec datocms migrations:run --destination=<sandbox-name> --api-token=<TOKEN>
```

Point local webpage to sandbox via `.envrc.personal`.

### Step 4: Promote to Production

1. Notify `#team-growth-marketing` with date/time
2. Enable maintenance: `pnpm exec datocms maintenance:on --api-token=<TOKEN>`
3. Run: `pnpm exec datocms migrations:run --destination=new-main --fast-fork --api-token=<TOKEN>`
4. Promote: `pnpm exec datocms environments:promote <sandbox-name> --api-token=<TOKEN>`
5. Disable maintenance: `pnpm exec datocms maintenance:off --api-token=<TOKEN>`
6. Notify channel

---

## Critical Gotchas

### Missing locale keys destroy data

When updating a localized field, missing locale keys = DatoCMS **deletes those locales permanently**.
**Always include ALL locales in update payloads for localized fields.**

### Block IDs are environment-scoped

Block IDs from one environment cannot be used in another. Strip `id` and `meta` from block envelopes when copying across environments.

### INVALID_LOCALES cascade

DatoCMS validates ALL locale-hash fields on PUT, not just changed ones. Normalize all locale-hash fields when fixing locale errors.

### section_id regex trips unrelated updates

The `section_id` field has a regex constraint (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$`). Dirty pre-existing data will reject even unrelated field updates.

### Pagination with nested records

`nested: true` caps at 30 per page. Always use `listPagedIterator`.

---

## Migration Utilities (`utils/`)

| Utility | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `resilientUpdate.ts` | Wraps `client.items.update()` with retry logic for 422 errors |
| `localization.ts` | Helpers for constructing locale hashes across all locales |
| `blocks.ts` | Block tree traversal (caveat: only follows first locale path) |
| `formMigration.ts` | Form-specific migration helpers |

---

## Validation

- Run migration in a fresh sandbox, verify schema in DatoCMS UI
- Point local webpage to sandbox, verify site renders
- Check `schema_migration` model to confirm migration was recorded
- `pnpm dev` against sandbox to catch frontend breakage
